    "body": "## Overview\n\nAdds a short note to the Online Benchmark example in `docs/benchmarking/cli.md`: `--base-url` must point at the server root **without** a `/v1` suffix, otherwise every request 404s.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Documentation-only change (7 lines); no code touched.\n- Documents a currently-undocumented footgun: `--base-url http://localhost:8000/v1` makes the tool resolve paths like `/v1/v1/completions`, so all requests fail with `404 Not Found` and the benchmark reports zero successful requests.\n\n## Validation\n\nReproduced on vLLM 0.32.0 (WSL2, single GPU) against a running `vllm serve`:\n\n```bash\n# server running on 127.0.0.1:8000\nvllm bench serve --backend openai --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1 \\\n  --model <served-name> --tokenizer <path> --dataset-name random \\\n  --num-prompts 4 --request-rate inf --max-concurrency 2\n# → Successful requests: 0, Failed requests: 4 (all \"Not Found\")\n\n# same command with --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8000 → runs normally\n```\n\nDirect `curl` to both `/v1/completions` and `/v1/chat/completions` on the same server returns 200, confirming the 404s come from the doubled prefix, not the server.\n\n## Details\n\n`vllm bench serve` appends the API routes itself, so a base URL that already ends in `/v1` duplicates the prefix. Nothing in the current benchmarking docs mentions this (the examples use default host/port and never show `--base-url`). Kept as a `!!! note` next to the first `vllm bench serve` example, matching the file's existing admonition style.\n\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Doc-only, no core impact.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Repro steps above; doc build renders the note.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Matches existing admonition style in the file.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Summary + evidence + root cause included.\n",
